  // BEGIN the-pqnk-framework-for-regenerative-animal-husbandry
  "the-pqnk-framework-for-regenerative-animal-husbandry": [
    { type: "imageGroup", files: ["kp114-img-01.jpg"] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "The journey of our food from farm to table is broken. The rise of debates like A1 versus A2 milk is not the problem, but a symptom of a deeper crisis: the collapse of our agricultural ecosystems. This paper moves beyond isolated issues to present a holistic framework for restoring health, wealth, and sustainability to animal husbandry through the principles of PQNK." }] },
    { type: "heading", text: "I. The Flawed Debate: A Symptom of a Broken System" },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "The science distinguishing A1 and A2 beta-casein proteins is valid, yet focusing on it alone is a distraction. The core determinant of milk's quality and health impact is not genetics alone, but the " }, { text: "health of the entire production ecosystem.", bold: true }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "An unhealthy A2 cow in a stressed, industrial setting will produce inflammatory milk due to cortisol, imbalanced fats, and chemical residues. A healthy, grass-fed A1 cow can produce milk that is better tolerated. True quality is a function of the entire system—from soil to soul." }] },
    { type: "heading", text: "II. The Pillars of PQNK: Principles for a New Paradigm" },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "PQNK is built on managing the farm as a living, interconnected system. Its principles are the non-negotiable foundation for producing truly nourishing food:" }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Soil Health is the Absolute Priority:", bold: true }, { text: " Living, microbially rich, mineral-dense soil is the only foundation for nutrient-dense forage." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Diverse Forage is the Engine:", bold: true }, { text: " A variety of grasses, legumes, and herbs (e.g., Napier, Alfalfa) provide the phytonutrients that translate into rich milk and robust animal health." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Native Breeds are the Ideal Conversion Machines:", bold: true }, { text: " Adapted over millennia, breeds like the " }, { text: "Gir", bold: true }, { text: " (renowned for disease resistance and rich milk) and " }, { text: "Sahiwal", bold: true }, { text: " (a dairy champion for arid regions) are unparalleled in their efficiency at converting diverse forage into nutritionally dense milk, not just high volume." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Animal Welfare is a Prerequisite:", bold: true }, { text: " Animals must express natural behaviors: grazing (minimum 2+ hours daily), freedom of movement, access to clean water and air, and a low-stress environment." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Embrace Natural Cycles:", bold: true }, { text: " Milk composition changes throughout lactation to meet the calf's needs. Respecting this cycle is respecting biological integrity." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Closed-Loop Economics:", bold: true }, { text: " The system is designed for internal reliance, recycling nutrients, and breaking dependence on external purchases." }] },
    { type: "heading", text: "III. The Economic Reality: The PQNK Advantage" },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "The misconception that ecological farming is less productive is overturned by a true cost analysis. PQNK shifts the economics from " }, { text: "High Input, High Output, Low Margin", bold: true }, { text: " to " }, { text: "Low Input, Moderate Output, High Margin.", bold: true }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "The PQNK Edge:", bold: true }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Stocking Density:", bold: true }, { text: " " }, { text: "~15 animals per acre", bold: true }, { text: " is achievable on managed, high-yield PQNK forage, vs. " }, { text: "~3 animals/acre", bold: true }, { text: " in traditional practices." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Input Costs:", bold: true }, { text: " " }, { text: "Substantially Lower.", bold: true }, { text: " Pasture management replaces purchased feed. Preventative health eliminates medicine costs." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Profitability:", bold: true }, { text: " " }, { text: "Highest.", bold: true }, { text: " Low production costs combined with premium prices for nutritionally dense, ethically produced milk sold directly to consumers ensure superior margins." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Resilience:", bold: true }, { text: " Immune to market shocks from input price fluctuations." }] },
    { type: "heading", text: "IV. A Classification of Animal Husbandry Systems" },
    { type: "imageGroup", files: ["kp114-img-02.jpg"] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "The following table contrasts the prevailing models, illustrating the logical progression towards the PQNK - Natural Ecosystem Science for Production Agriculture:" }] },
    { type: "heading", text: "V. A Call to Collective Action" },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "The path forward requires a collective shift in mindset." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "To Farmers:", bold: true }, { text: " You are the stewards of this transition. Embrace your role as ecosystem managers. Prioritize soil health, animal welfare, and native genetics. Your path to lasting prosperity lies in the value and resilience of the PQNK model." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "To Consumers:", bold: true }, { text: " You hold the power of choice. Inquire beyond labels. " }, { text: "Ask: \"How was the animal raised?\" \"What did it eat?\"", bold: true }, { text: " Your demand for truly healthy food empowers farmers to adopt these practices and rebuild our agricultural ecology." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "Conclusion:", bold: true }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "We stand at a crossroads. We can continue to debate single molecules within a broken system, or we can choose to heal the system itself. The PQNK framework offers a proven, profitable, and regenerative path forward—one that restores the true value of milk and meat by honoring the health of the soil, the animal, the farmer, and the consumer." }] },
    { type: "paragraph", runs: [{ text: "In service of the ecosystem," }] },
    { type: "heading", text: "The PQNK Team" },
    { type: "heading", text: "www.Facebook.Com/Pedaver" },
    { type: "heading", text: "https://www.youtube.com/@pedaverpqnk3167/videos" },
    { type: "heading", text: "pedaver@gmail.com" },
    { type: "heading", text: "WhatsApp +92 320 677 6666" },
  ],
